{{!-- Tags as the book prints them: italic text, comma-separated, inline in the row. Context:
      `tags` = a ResolvedTag[] (see src/model/data/Tags.js). Used wherever tags are DISPLAYED —
      inventory rows, arcanum cards, follower and NPC cards; the editable chip picker is
      selection-chips.hbs.

      A defined tag is a real <button> because core binds click for [data-action] only, so a
      clickable span would be keyboard-dead — but it is styled back down to plain italic text
      (.stonetop-tag), because a control in the middle of a sentence is not what the book shows.
      `data-tooltip` is pointer-only and invisible to assistive tech, so the definition also rides on
      aria-label. `data-view-state` keeps the button live on a non-editable sheet, which otherwise
      disables every button it renders.

      The comma sits BETWEEN the elements, never inside the button — it is punctuation, not part of
      the tag, and it must not be clickable or underlined.

      NO trailing newline: a partial renders its whole file, so one would land as a space inside the
      caller's parenthetical ("close , x piercing"). --}}
<span class="stonetop-tag-list">
	{{~#each tags~}}
		{{~#if hasDefinition~}}
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-tag is-defined" data-action="showTagDefinition"
			        data-view-state data-tag="{{slug}}" data-definition="{{definition}}"
			        data-tooltip="{{definition}}"
			        aria-label="{{label}} — {{definition}}">{{label}}</button>
		{{~else~}}
			<span class="stonetop-tag">{{label}}</span>
		{{~/if~}}
		{{~#unless @last}}, {{/unless~}}
	{{~/each~}}</span>